; Practical module guides. Keybindings is the source of saved hotkey assignments.
class ModuleHelp {
    static Introduction(id) {
        switch id {
            case "cascade-kingdom":
                return "WHY I MADE THIS"
                    . "`r`nI wanted an easier way to manage lots of open windows: keep them large "
                    . "and neatly organized, switch between them effortlessly, and avoid digging "
                    . "through a messy pile of overlapping windows."
                    . "`r`n`r`nCASCADE ONLY WHEN YOU ASK"
                    . "`r`nHold the cascade key while launching to add a new window. Settings "
                    . "lets you choose CapsLock or Pause; enable Secret Layers and the selected key. "
                    . "You can release the key before it finishes opening. With automatic cascading "
                    . "enabled, hold the same key to open normally instead. All displays uses the "
                    . "launch-pointer display; selecting one display sends new cascade windows there."
                    . "`r`n`r`nFOCUS TABS"
                    . "`r`nClick a focus tab to select a slot. Click again to cycle windows sharing "
                    . "that slot. Dragging an eligible window shows opaque corner guides on "
                    . "valid destination slots. Align its top-left corner and release to join; "
                    . "resizing does not adopt windows. Choose guide and tab colors in Settings."
                    . "`r`n`r`nADOPT AN EXISTING WINDOW"
                    . "`r`nHold the selected key and double-click a title bar to adopt the window, "
                    . "even in automatic mode. The adopt action in Keybindings is independent. "
                    . "A selected destination redirects adoption too. Dragging to an excluded "
                    . "display leaves the window there, outside the cascade. A disconnected "
                    . "selected display pauses new adoption until it returns or you change Settings."
            case "wonder-windows":
                return "WHY I MADE THIS"
                    . "`r`nWindows already has window-management shortcuts, but I found many of them "
                    . "frustrating or incomplete. I wanted something more powerful, consistent "
                    . "and predictable, without constantly reaching for the mouse."
                    . "`r`n`r`nARRANGE YOUR WINDOWS"
                    . "`r`nUse the left and right layout actions to cycle through positions such as "
                    . "quarter-width, half-width and near-center. Corner and top/bottom tiles offer "
                    . "more precise placement. Stretch toward neighboring windows or cycle "
                    . "between full-height and full-width. Restore brings back the original shape."
                    . "`r`n`r`nFOCUS, SWAP AND FULLSCREEN"
                    . "`r`nMove focus to the nearest window in a direction, swap with another window, "
                    . "or temporarily minimize a group. Win + Enter cycles overlapping windows "
                    . "without moving them, while Caps + Win + Arrows swaps with nearby windows. "
                    . "Win + Up cycles between maximized and half-height positions. Moving a "
                    . "window to another display preserves cascade membership only where cascading is allowed. Layout "
                    . "shortcuts exit F11 fullscreen before repositioning a window. The isolate "
                    . "action hides other windows in a group; use it again to restore them."
            case "power-up-utilities":
                return "WHY I MADE THIS"
                    . "`r`nI wanted a collection of practical shortcuts for everyday tasks that "
                    . "didn't fit into the other modules."
                    . "`r`n`r`nMORE KEYS WITHOUT A NEW KEYBOARD"
                    . "`r`nSend F13-F24 or Numpad 0-9 using shortcuts, even if your keyboard "
                    . "doesn't have those keys. The virtual numpad is especially useful on "
                    . "compact keyboards without a number pad, while F13-F24 provides extra "
                    . "keys for shortcuts in compatible applications. Held virtual keys are "
                    . "released when you release their triggering hotkey."
                    . "`r`n`r`nTEXT AND TERMINAL ACTIONS"
                    . "`r`nInsert punctuation, special spaces or a yyyyMMdd-HHmmss timestamp. "
                    . "Terminal copy and clear operate only in Windows Terminal. "
                    . "Required Terminal shortcuts are checked before keys are sent; "
                    . "incompatible settings are reported without being changed. "
                    . "Text commands wait for your triggering keys to be released before typing."
                    . "`r`n`r`nSYSTEM UTILITIES"
                    . "`r`nWake speakers that automatically enter standby, or put your computer "
                    . "to sleep."
            case "paper-pad":
                return "WHY I MADE THIS"
                    . "`r`nI wanted a place to quickly jot down anything, anytime, without "
                    . "worrying about saving files or finding notes buried in windows and tabs. "
                    . "Something I could open and hide instantly, easily switch between notes, "
                    . "and keep my ideas organized and separate from the clutter of everyday project work."
                    . "`r`n`r`nYOUR OWN QUICK-NOTES DRAWER"
                    . "`r`nPaper Pad opens a dedicated Notepad3 window without taking over your "
                    . "ordinary editor sessions. Use Open pad below or the configurable toggle "
                    . "hotkey. Notepad3's Ctrl + N creates a timestamped page automatically. "
                    . "Page navigation shortcuts work only inside the editor."
                    . "`r`n`r`nPAGES ARE REAL FILES"
                    . "`r`nNew pages receive timestamped filenames. They remain ordinary files "
                    . "in your notes folder, and Save As can rename a page within that folder. "
                    . "If you type before a native New is attached, use Save As to preserve it. "
                    . "Hiding Paper Pad preserves undo history, but switching pages clears it. "
                    . "You can still inspect and back up these files in an ordinary file manager."
                    . "`r`n`r`nSAVING AND RELOADING"
                    . "`r`nPaper Pad automatically saves changes when switching pages, hiding or exiting. "
                    . "Settings lets you choose your Notepad3 executable, notes folder, display "
                    . "and drawer size. Changing paths never moves existing notes. "
                    . "Notepad3 controls external-file reloads, which may replace unsaved text."
            case "secret-layers":
                return "WHY I MADE THIS"
                    . "`r`nI wanted to get more out of my existing keyboard. CapsLock and Pause seemed "
                    . "like perfect candidates for unlocking an entirely new set of shortcuts "
                    . "without adding more keys."
                    . "`r`n`r`nHOLD A KEY FOR MORE HOTKEYS"
                    . "`r`nHold CapsLock or Pause, then press another key to run its assigned action. "
                    . "A short tap instead arms the next key for 1.4 seconds, so you don't need "
                    . "to hold both keys at once. Tap the same key again to cancel the layer or "
                    . "trigger an assigned double-tap action. Only one layer can be active at a time."
                    . "`r`n`r`nTOGGLE CAPS LOCK"
                    . "`r`nDouble-tap Shift (by default) to toggle Caps Lock while its layer "
                    . "is enabled. You can choose Ctrl or Alt instead, or disable this feature "
                    . "in Settings. Only two quick taps of the same modifier count, without "
                    . "another key in between. You can also assign a shortcut in Keybindings."
        }
        return ""
    }

    static Text(id, manager) => this.Introduction(id)
}
